The quick buttons on the home screen got a fifth one in the middle, with banknotes. Behind it is Togetherly Wallet, our app for a couple's shared budget. Until it launches, the button opens a receipt: what Wallet does and how many people are already waiting. Tap "Join the waitlist" and you will get a notification on launch day, and the same button will open Wallet.

The days counter no longer falls a day behind at night. The home timer, profile, stats and the "Days together" widget count the same way, and after midnight the widget moves to the new day on its own.

Deleting an account can now be undone for a week: just sign in again. The pair, memories and chat stay in place all week.

Widgets are readable on every theme, the fill picks its tone to suit the text. "Year ring" looks the same on iPhone and Android, the halves of the pair widget on iPhone are equal again, and a widget placed before pairing switches to the pair by itself.

The shared chat background is saved and seen by both, and a purchased background survives an iPhone update.

The watch-together room on a phone tells you why a video did not start instead of a silent button.

A drawing keeps its proportions on the second phone, erased strokes do not come back, the camera flips in video notes and their cover no longer gets lost. The time capsule takes letters up to 10,000 characters.

The Togetherly+ showcase appears at most once per visit, the "How to help yourself" tips are shown in full, and nothing runs off narrow screens with large fonts.
